  "notes": "STOP. B2 (dynamic ACL with dependency propagation, rechecked at cache serve, future read, and queued execution) has zero unauthorized deliveries and executions on the deterministic cases, and it still allows every still-authorized request. B3 is the real ReleaseGate reserve plus commit recheck: it cancels an in-flight release of asset-a when with_policy_version bumps asset-a, including the owner's still-lawful in-flight release (false reject, fail closed on the epoch). The same recheck does not stop a summary that was registered as derived-a with a copied tutoring grant, because commit compares derived-a's own policy version. B0 keeps the T0 snapshot. B1 re-reads the grant but treats a derived object as uncontrolled data, so subject-r receives derived-a after revocation. B4 inherits a static confidentiality label and same-org clearance, so revocation and per-principal grants are invisible. The candidate cross_module_coordinator is not developed; it is B2. Dev-scan rates are illustrative only. Deterministic B2 violation_rate=0.000, task_success=1.000, false_reject=0.000. Dev-scan B2 violations=0/5.",
